Task 3: Implement controlled object spawning
Improve the spawning system so objects appear at varied horizontal positions and at varied intervals, rather than a fixed interval with a plain random x each time. Make sure objects never spawn outside the playable area, avoid repeatedly spawning in the same spot, and cap how many objects can be on screen at once so the game never becomes unplayable.]. Replace the fixed spawn interval with a random interval range, keep spawn x within [radius, WIDTH - radius], avoid spawning within N pixels of the last spawn x, and cap max objects on screen (e.g. 6). Keep the code simple and readable.

Ran a command, shared files
Updated game_engine.py with controlled spawning. Only the engine changed.

Random intervals: the timer resets to a random value between MIN_SPAWN_INTERVAL (30) and MAX_SPAWN_INTERVAL (70) frames.
Inside the screen: spawn x is picked from [OBJECT_RADIUS, WIDTH - OBJECT_RADIUS].
No repeat spots: _pick_spawn_x re-rolls up to 10 times if the new x is within MIN_SPAWN_DISTANCE (60px) of the last spawn. After 10 tries it accepts whatever it has, so it can never loop forever.
Cap: if MAX_OBJECTS (6) are already on screen, that spawn is skipped and the timer still resets.
All the tuning values are constants at the top of the file. I used OBJECT_RADIUS = 14 to match the earlier spawn height and the default in collision.py. If FallingObject has its own radius, change the constant to match.

