Task 4: Add a temporary basket speed boost
Add a speed-boost mechanic the player can activate during play that temporarily increases the basket's movement speed. Show a clear indication while the boost is active, and have the basket automatically return to normal speed once it expires.. Use the existing boosted_frames, normal_speed, boost_speed fields in Basket. Activate the boost with the SPACE key (in handle_keydown), last ~3 seconds at 60 FPS, add a cooldown if you think it's needed, show a visible indicator while active (e.g. text "BOOST!" plus a basket color change in the renderer), and revert speed automatically

Ran a command, shared files
The speed boost is in. Three files changed: basket.py, renderer.py and game_engine.py.

How it works

Activation: SPACE in handle_keydown calls basket.activate_boost(180), which sets boosted_frames to 180 (about 3 seconds at 60 FPS) and switches speed to boost_speed.
Speed: boost_speed is now speed * 2 (10 px/frame instead of 5). Change that line in Basket.__init__ if you want a different multiplier.
Expiry: basket.update_boost() runs once per frame in update(). When the counter reaches 0, speed goes back to normal_speed.
Cooldown: I added a 5-second cooldown that starts when the boost ends. Without it, the player could keep the boost on almost permanently by tapping SPACE. It's BOOST_COOLDOWN_FRAMES at the top of the engine file.
Indicator: while boosted, the basket turns gold and "BOOST! 2.4s" shows under the miss counter. Otherwise that spot shows either "Boost cooldown: Xs" or "Boost ready (SPACE)".
The game over screen blocks boosting, and pressing R resets everything, including the cooldown.

The game_engine.py you uploaded this time was the version with only Task 1 applied. I kept building on my copy, which has Tasks 1 to 3 included, so use the new file as the replacement. If you'd rather keep your own Task 2 and 3 changes, you'll need to merge them in.

I only syntax-checked these, since I couldn't run the game here. Hold SPACE once to confirm the timing feels right. If 3 seconds is too long or short, change BOOST_DURATION_FRAMES.


